    {
      "title": "CROX: Exceptional Business at a Puzzling Discount",
      "fund": "r/ValueInvesting",
      "date": "April 22, 2025",
      "summary": "The deep dive emphasizes the massive market disconnect between Crocs' best-in-class financial performance\u201428% ROIC, 57% gross margins, and a 22% FCF margin converting $923M in annual free cash flow\u2014and its depressed valuation of ~6x EV/EBITDA. The post dismantles bear cases around tariffs and fashion fatigue by highlighting the brand's low manufacturing costs and flexible outsourced supply chain. Operational catalysts include reducing net debt-to-EBITDA below 1.5x, re-igniting HEYDUDE DTC channels, and executing on a $1.3B authorized share repurchase program.",
